        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Why the PAGI spec is moving to Perl 5.24]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[The PAGI specification and the tools related to it are increasing the minimum Perl version to 5.24. This change is largely due to updates from its major dependencies (Future) and needs to fix problematic features such as the cancellation of asynchronous methods, leading to this clean break and avoiding using shadow methods that were reliant on the previous versions. Thus, anyone with an older version of Perl is invited to prepare for an upgrade.]]></description>
            <pubDate>2026.10.22</pubDate>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://dev.to/jjn1056/why-the-pagi-spec-is-moving-to-perl-524-58ne</guid>
            <link>https://dev.to/jjn1056/why-the-pagi-spec-is-moving-to-perl-524-58ne</link>
            
            
            
            <author><![CDATA[john_napiorkowski]]></author>
            
                
            
            
        </item>
        
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Apache2::Request: Fixing the build]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Rob has made available version 2.18 of libapreq2 (via a new fork of Apache2::Request), thus rescuing the now-defunct library from the incompatible builds of the latest CPAN installers (cpm / cpanm). The update resolves issues with the MakeMaker arguments, creates metadata, and fixes the test suite, thus making old installations of mod_perl work successfully again.]]></description>
            <pubDate>2026.10.23</pubDate>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://blog.tbcdevelopmentgroup.com/2026-10-23-post.html</guid>
            <link>https://blog.tbcdevelopmentgroup.com/2026-10-23-post.html</link>
            
            
            
            <author><![CDATA[rob_lauer]]></author>
            
                
            
            
        </item>
        
